<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mexican Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mexican Revolution was the series of revolts and civil wars that began in November 1910 with Francisco Madero's call to rise against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porfirio-diaz">Porfirio Díaz</a>. After Díaz fell, revolutionary leaders including Carranza, Obregón, Villa and Zapata fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta">Victoriano Huerta</a> and then one another, at the cost of hundreds of thousands of lives. It produced the Constitution of 1917, land reform and the long rule of the party that became the PRI.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution.jpg" alt="Mexican Revolution" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osuna · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Decena_tr%C3%A1gica.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
